From 6de1254283aeafb4004727f6ca6ecdfc7d84e431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:24:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 45/85] feat(beacon): beacon_trusted_relays lets a named relay
 vouch for hosts

A relay that re-sends another host's beacon from its own address was
always dropped as url_mismatch. beacon_trusted_relays lists relays by
source address with the hosts (IPv4 or CIDR, RFC1918 only) each may
advertise. Relayed datagrams keep every other check: RFC1918 source,
arrival interface, own-beacon filter, table cap. A relay gets a larger
source bucket, while each host it speaks for is limited as if it beaconed
directly, and one relay lists at most 16 hosts.

/health beacon_listener shows via on relayed hosts, echoes
trusted_relays, and counts relayed_accepted, relayed_refreshed and
relay_host_refused. Default [] keeps the strict behaviour. Changes apply
at runtime; removing a relay drops the hosts it vouched for.

